WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.959
This is the Week 9 deck: flat, 96 × 32 mm. Now we'll add kicktails, so the nose and tail tip up like a real board.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:15.349
Keep your Week 9 deck safe. Click + at the bottom left → Create Part Studio.

00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:21.890
Rename the tab Kicktail Deck. Units are already mm: they belong to the whole document.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:31.321
Variables belong to one Part Studio, so make #hole again here: 2.3 mm, bolt + clearance.

00:00:31.871 --> 00:00:42.936
Sketch on the Front plane, press N. Draw the deck from the side: press L, click the left tip, both bends, and the right tip.

00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:48.466
Three lines: a flat middle through the origin, and a kick on each end.

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:54.926
Dimension the flat middle: 62 mm. That keeps every bolt hole on flat deck.

00:00:55.476 --> 00:00:57.972
Each kick is 17 mm long.

00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:08.414
Kick angle: click the kick and the flat line, move until the small angle shows, type 24.5°.

00:01:08.964 --> 00:01:14.060
Same on the other side: 17 long, 24.5°.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:21.124
Round each bend with the sketch fillet: click the corner, type 8. A smooth bend is stronger.

00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:24.344
Both bends are rounded. Finish the sketch.

00:01:24.894 --> 00:01:32.661
Shift+E → Thin tab. Thin turns lines into a solid with a set thickness. Click the sketch in the list.

00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:40.525
Thickness 2.5 mm. Check Symmetric, so the deck grows out to both sides of the Front plane.

00:01:41.075 --> 00:01:43.641
Depth 32: that's the deck width.

00:01:44.191 --> 00:01:47.744
Now it's a bent slab with kicks, but the ends are still square.

00:01:48.294 --> 00:01:55.167
Sketch on the Top plane, press N. Draw the outline from the top, the Lesson 2.1 way.

00:01:55.717 --> 00:02:02.811
A center-point rectangle out to where the bends start, and a circle on each end, sized to the corners.

00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:10.129
The rectangle snaps to the deck edges, so it's fully defined: 32 wide.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:17.123
Extrude with Intersect. Intersect keeps only the deck that's inside the outline.

00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:22.282
Through all + Symmetric, so it cuts all the way up through the kicks.

00:02:22.832 --> 00:02:26.327
There it is: rounded nose and tail, kicked up.

00:02:26.877 --> 00:02:34.574
Holes, same as Week 9. Sketch on the flat top face. Press R, follow the yellow dotted line.

00:02:35.124 --> 00:02:40.325
25 from the origin, 8 along, 6 across. Use your own truck numbers.

00:02:40.875 --> 00:02:43.696
Mirror across the Right plane for the second truck.

00:02:44.246 --> 00:02:47.799
Hole tool: Simple, diameter #hole, Through all.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:54.026
Click all eight corners. Every hole is on the flat middle, so the trucks mount flat.

00:02:54.576 --> 00:03:02.390
The kicktail deck: 32 wide, 2.5 thick, 24.5° kicks, 8 holes.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.595
From the side you see the kicks. It can't lie flat on the printer.

00:03:08.145 --> 00:03:16.203
Right-click the part → Export → 3MF. When you submit, tell your teacher: supports under the kicks.
